## 6. Integration Notes

### For Claude Code
- Implement `SurvivorStats.cs` with int fields clamped to `[1, 100]`
- Implement `LevelSystem.cs` using formula: `(level * 100) + (Mathf.Pow(level, 2) * 10)`
- Implement `PerkSystem.cs` with prime number detection for unlock triggers
- Implement `CharacterType.cs` as an enum with all 30 types defined
- Use `ScriptableObject` per character type to define starting stat values
- Fire `OnPerkUnlocked` event when level hits a prime number
- Fire `OnLevelUp` event each time XP threshold is crossed
- Fire `OnCharacterTypeAssigned` on survivor creation to apply type bonuses

### For Claude Design
- Stat bars display as 1–100 filled progress bars
- Perk unlock screen appears automatically at prime number levels
- Perk selection UI shows 3 randomized options with descriptions
- Level progress bar shows XP toward next prime and next level separately
- Character type selector displays all 30 types with role descriptions on creation screen
- Each character type card shows its primary role and stat bonus preview
